DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ggxxddiittvviieeww  program  displays  the  _g_r_o_f_f  _i_n_t_e_r_m_e_d_i_a_t_e _o_u_t_p_u_t, see
       ggrrooffff__oouutt(5), on an X display.  It uses the standard X11 fonts,  so  it
       does  not require access to the server machine for font loading.  There
       are several ways to use ggxxddiittvviieeww.

       The _g_r_o_f_f _i_n_t_e_r_m_e_d_i_a_t_e _o_u_t_p_u_t can be generated by ggrrooffff --ZZ.   This  can
       be  viewed by explicitly calling ggxxddiittvviieeww _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e.  If _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e is --,
       ggxxddiittvviieeww will read the standard input;  _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e  cannot  be  omitted.
       The  _g_r_o_f_f _i_n_t_e_r_m_e_d_i_a_t_e _o_u_t_p_u_t is different for all devices.  ggxxddiittvviieeww
       can view it for all devices, but the quality is device dependent.

       The best results are achieved with the XX* devices  for  ggrrooffff's  option
       --TT.   There  are  four  XX* devices: --TTXX7755, --TTXX7755--1122, --TTXX110000, --TTXX110000--1122.
       They differ by the X resolution (75dpi or 100dpi)  and  the  used  base
       font  size  (10pt  or  12pt).  They are especially built for ggxxddiittvviieeww.
       When using one of them ggrrooffff generates the _i_n_t_e_r_m_e_d_i_a_t_e _o_u_t_p_u_t for this
       device  and calls ggxxddiittvviieeww automatically for viewing.  For example, to
       view this man page with a base resolution of 12pt, say

              ggrrooffff --TTXX110000--1122 --mmaann --rrSS1122 ggxxddiittvviieeww..11

       (option --rrSS_X_X is documented in the ggrrooffff__mmaann(7) man page).

       ggrrooffff's option --XX produces _i_n_t_e_r_m_e_d_i_a_t_e _o_u_t_p_u_t for the  _P_o_s_t_S_c_r_i_p_t  de‐
       vice  and  subsequently uses ggxxddiittvviieeww as a viewer for it.  The quality
       of the result depends mainly on the chosen point size and display reso‐
       lution; for rapid previewing, however, something like

              ggrrooffff --XX --PP--rreessoolluuttiioonn --PP110000 _d_o_c_u_m_e_n_t

